    "chunk_size_bytes": 1876,
    "chunk_text": "This morning, we met the Hon. Speaker and raised our concerns. The Hon. Speaker was good enough to convene a Party Leaders' Meeting a little while ago. Hon. Presiding Member, this Debate is illegal; it is contrary to the Standing Orders. The Standing Orders very clearly state that the relevant Sectoral Oversight Committee must give its Report and it is only after that Report that anything must be moved in Parliament. It is true that the\n\n47 48\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0da9\u0dd3.\u0db6\u0dd3.\u0dc0\u0dda\u0d9a\u0dae\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dca\u0dc0\u0db8 \u0d9a\u0dad\u0dc0]\n\n2014\u0dc0\u0da2\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dc0\u0db4\u0dad\u0dc013\n\nAt the Party Leaders' Meeting, it was told that this is the practice, this is how all reports are. But, that is not true. We had another Report presented today in this House. I am comparing the two Reports. The other Report is by the Committee on Public Finance. Out of the two Reports, one states that the Report will be submitted. The Report of Committee on Public Finance is an actual report. In that, there is an introduction, Orders under Section 2 of the Special Commodity Levy Act, the observations and the recommendations made by the Committee. So, like that, one by one, everything has been considered and finally, the decision of the Committee is given. That is a report, not what has been tabled here calling itself a \"Report\", which states that a Report will be submitted by the Chairman of the Committee. So, this is an illegal Debate. Merely because there are more numbers on the Government benches, it does not mean that this is a report. What we have demonstrated to the country today is that the Members who voted a little while ago cannot read; it exposes to the country the literacy of the Government Members. The Government Members have said that this is a report when, in fact, it is not. The whole country must know that these people who cannot even read are the ones on the Government benches today."
