    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0665bdc8de55e7a56916352253d09d66",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1792,
    "chunk_text": "So says Mr. Parakala Prabhakar. He is none other than the husband of the current Finance Minister of India, Nirmala Sitharaman. He is a forthright man; he is a revered critic in Indian circles. So, he says that. That is exactly what is going to happen here as well.\n\n55 56\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dc0\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dae\u0dc0\u0d9a\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca\u0dc0\u0db8 \u0d9a\u0dad\u0dc0]\n\n2014\u0dc0\u0da2\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dc0\u0db4\u0dad\u0dc013\n\nIt has always been applied in the breach. So, Article 3 of the ICCPR Act is there, if you want to control hate speech. Then, there are Sections 6 and 17 of the Computer Crimes Act. They, too, deal with some of the issues in cyber space. Section 2 of the Obscene Publications Ordinance already has certain provisions to deal with obscene publications. Then, using the Electronic Transactions Act, some of the transactions that the Hon. Kanaka Herath seems to be complaining about on the digital platforms, the misuse of them, could also be dealt with. We have recently enacted that legislation. So, there are several such available avenues, Bills that have already been passed by this House, but this Act is going to further the horizon or the scope. So, that is why we wanted some additional time to properly study the implications of this Bill on freedom of expression in this country and the democratic space in this country, which is getting narrower and narrower with the harsh, high-handed actions by our law and order machinery and the law enforcement machinery.\n\nYesterday, Prof. Savitri Goonesekere, in a discussion where the Hon. (Prof.) G.L. Peiris and various others also participated, was very harshly commenting on this. She is a highly respected senior professor of law. She was also very critical about the purpose for which this Bill is being brought, saying it is very suspicious."
  },
