    "chunk_size_bytes": 1169,
    "chunk_text": "This Bill was gazetted on the 15th of September, 2023 and 46 petitions were filed against it. When the case came up in the Supreme Court, on the very first day, the Attorney-General presented 31 Amendments. This is a Bill which has 57 Clauses and Amendments were proposed to over 50 per cent of those Clauses by the Attorney-General. The petitioners were not informed of those amendments and the lawyers appearing for the petitioners were not given any time to discuss the amendments with their clients. The case went on for three days without any discussion or a chance being given for those citizens who petitioned the court against the Bill to examine or discuss the Amendments proposed by the Attorney-General on the first day itself. So, it is there that the first violation of this legislative process occurred. So, a proper judicial oversight was denied and the opportunity for the public to object to the amended Bill was also denied.\n\n221 222\n\n\u0db4\u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\n\nSectoral Oversight Committee. So, once again, it is very clear that the Sectoral Oversight Committee was simply used as a tool to bring this Bill forward for its Second Reading."
