    "chunk_size_bytes": 1842,
    "chunk_text": "So, this Bill has nothing to do with protecting women and children. Already there are laws, existing laws - even the civil law was recently amended - that anyone can take action against defamation. The necessary laws are already present in our judicial system. The problem is not the lack of laws, but the implementation of the laws. If the Minister takes the trouble to actually talk to women and children who have faced this problem in this country, who have faced not just online abuse, but even physical abuse and harassment, the treatment that is meted out by the police, the very Department that the Minister looks after, he would get an understanding that it is not the lack of laws that is preventing justice from being meted out to women and children or protection of women and children in this country, but the lack of institutional or cultural change within the police which enables them to deal with the issues of women and children in a sensitive manner. There are many stories of how women and children are\n\ntreated by the police of this country. So, this is not because of the lack of laws; this is to do with their attitude, lack of resources and lack of leadership.\n\nHowever, when there are such competing demands, we need to be extremely careful about which of those rights we uphold and how we balance those many rights that, as an Assembly, we are committed to protect.\n\nI also want to say this. If this Government thinks that bringing in these types of laws is going to thwart the will of the people, that it is going to crush the voice of the people, I think they are making a huge mistake. I repeat, they are making a huge mistake. If they want to win over the people, then they have to look into themselves,\n\n223 224\n\n\u0dad\u0dab\u0dd4\u0dc0 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dd2\u0dba \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0dd2 \u0dc1\u0db8\u0dc1\u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbb\n\n2024 \u0da2\u0db1 \u0dc1\u0dd2 54"
  },
