    "chunk_size_bytes": 1641,
    "chunk_text": "He is someone who has a rounded personality. I have had the privilege of being involved with him even in sports outside this House and having come to this House, I have been able to see him as somebody who has served with such dedication for the last 42 years.\n\nHaving said that, I would like to read from \u201cParliament and its Sovereignty\u201d, a book in the Library and which talks about this famous event. In Chapter 5, \u201cThe Officers of Parliament\u201d, it states, I quote:\n\n\u201c......Charles I, miscalculating, thought that he could rely on Speaker Lenthall\u2019s support when he forced his way into the Commons to arrest the five Members. Lenthall to Charles\u2019s surprise showed that he interpreted his duty as owing obedience to the House rather than to the monarch. He said that he had \u2018neither eyes to see nor tongue to speak but as the House is pleased to direct\u2019.\u201d\n\nSo, with such events in the history and in the annals of the House of Commons, we, too, in line with those precious traditions, have to uphold the dignity and decorum of this House. In doing that very duty, Mr. Narendra Fernando has indeed served us well for the past 23 years in the Office of Serjeant-at-Arms. Of course, he was elevated to that office way back in 2018. But, he had been promoted to that office after serving so long as Assistant Serjeant-at-Arms and the Deputy Serjeant-at-Arms.\n\nSir, I wish him the very best in his retired life! \u0dd9\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Speaker) \u0dab\u0dd4\u0dc0 \u0dd2\u0dba\u0dc1 \u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dc1\u0db1\u0dc1 \u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc1."
  },
