    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1710996369012066.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2024-02-07-2024-02-07-0110",
    "chunk_index": 110,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b3a2487af065ea9470003c766cf65164",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2021,
    "chunk_text": "The 2024 Budget Proposals mark the initial stride in essential reforms aimed at propelling economic development. Despite challenges and occasional reluctance, the economic reforms and policies we have instituted have set us on the trajectory towards a stable economy, earning recognition from international financial institutions for our targeted approach.\n\nThe severe economic crisis of the past subjected many citizens to unimaginable hardships - job losses, income source depletion, missed business opportunities and disenfranchisement - most acutely felt by the common people. Presently, we are gradually restoring lost opportunities through initiatives like the \"Urumaya\" Programme, aiming to reinstate people's rights. Under the \u201cUrumaya\u201d Programme, which was initiated the day before yesterday, we focus on two fundamental objectives: one is land and the other is housing. The British Colonial Government, through the Waste Lands Ordinance in 1897, deprived people of their land rights, a grievance that went unaddressed by subsequent post-Independence administrations. We have initiated the process of granting them land rights, which is set to benefit over two million people. Enlisting two million new landowners into our society marks a historic and a revolutionary stride, an honour to the enduring struggles of farmers striving for self-sufficiency in rice production.\n\nApproximately one-third of our country's populace faces insufficient income and lacks suitable housing. Our\n\n29 30\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\ncommitment involves taking measures to provide these individuals with both income sources and a legacy of housing. Complete ownership of more than 50,000 houses will be granted to low-income urban residents.\n\nLaunching onto a successful economic development path demands special attention to all regions of the country, especially to the poor and vulnerable communities. Despite facing a severe economic crisis, we have consistently taken steps for the welfare of our citizens."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2024-02-07-2024-02-07",
