    "md5": "172d49fb1ead2ed3acdef8396a63d604",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1413,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, the President\u2019s Address the other day listed how he and his Government have succeeded in pulling this country out of a dangerous economic situation and went on to state what the Government intends doing in the future. The Speech was, more or less, directed to the voters of this country, presumably keeping the coming Presidential Election in view. Of course, such speeches, sometimes, do camouflage the real intention of the Government and its President, who may want to stage\n\nSir, there are a few matters that I wish to bring to the notice of the Hon. Members of this Assembly, which fall out from the President\u2019s Speech and which need your earnest attention. Firstly, the Hon. President has called upon the people to unite in the pursuit of our nation-building dream. Which nation does he refer to? Maybe the Sinhala nation only. What about the Tamil nation who have occupied the North and the East of this Island for over 3,000 years and still remain the majority in those areas? Shaking hands is possible, if both parties are firmly on terra firma as equals. A person standing at the bottom of the well cannot shake hands with those who are standing outside the well. He or she must be brought up from the bottom of the well to shake hands with those standing on terra firma. Thus, there is an urgent need, on the part of the President, to revitalize the forgotten people of the North and the East."
  },
