    "md5": "d5e907ed375bca8c10c540d224504ba2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, there are a few matters that I wish to bring to the notice of the Hon. Members of this Assembly, which fall out from the President\u2019s Speech and which need your earnest attention. Firstly, the Hon. President has called upon the people to unite in the pursuit of our nation-building dream. Which nation does he refer to? Maybe the Sinhala nation only. What about the Tamil nation who have occupied the North and the East of this Island for over 3,000 years and still remain the majority in those areas? Shaking hands is possible, if both parties are firmly on terra firma as equals. A person standing at the bottom of the well cannot shake hands with those who are standing outside the well. He or she must be brought up from the bottom of the well to shake hands with those standing on terra firma. Thus, there is an urgent need, on the part of the President, to revitalize the forgotten people of the North and the East.\n\nThe Hon. President has avoided speaking about the North and the East and its political problems, which remain unresolved. There is a tendency among Sinhala leaders to believe that the problems of the Tamil-speaking people were over with the end of the war. After treating the war as an insurrection by the Tamil youth, by continuing to pay all government servants in the North and the East during that time their monthly salaries and other dues, it is wrong for the Government to presume that the conflict was a total war between the Sinhalese and the Tamils. The political problems of the Tamils remain the same as before the start of the war and even after the end of the war. If the Government intends washing off its hands with regard to the Tamils of the North and the East, it must say so. We, Tamils, could work out some other device to help our suffering people. After all, the geopolitics of the times have placed before us many options.\n\n331 332\n\n\u0db4\u0da7\u0dbb\u0dca\u0d9a\u0ddc\u0dc1 \u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dc0"
