    "chunk_text": "Then, I would like to point out that there is an intrinsic link between agriculture, in particular in Sri Lanka\u2019s dry zone rice cultivation, and health epidemics. There is an unexpected increase in the number of disease cases in a specific geographical area. Here, the area is the dry zone of Sri Lanka. The root cause of the epidemics has been found to be toxicants such as arsenic, cadmium and lead found in fertilizers and also in weedicides and pesticides. The primary source of exposure to toxicants is the diet of our people, in particular rice, which is consumed at all meals. The country\u2019s national agriculture is intrinsically\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dc5 \u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, your time is over.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 . .\u0dc0\u0dd3. \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dda\u0db4\u0db1\u0dca \u0db1\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95.\u0bb5\u0bbf. \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0ba9\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. C.V. Wigneswaran) Give me just one more minute, Sir.\n\nIn Jaffna, we are giving priority to the making of organic fertilizers such as compost manure, sea weed, fertilizers from kitchen, fish meal, wood ash, liquid organic fertilizers, earthworm castings and others. We cannot immediately stop the importation of chemical fertilizers as done some time ago. But, as we progress along in our manufacture of organic fertilizers progressively, we could reduce and finally do away with the inorganic chemical fertilizers. Let me commit this matter to the attention of the Hon. President and the officials of the relevant departments. In this connection, I am beholden to Dr. Kamal Gammanpila who educated me with regard to the serious effect our fertilizers, weedicides and pesticides are having on the diet of our people.\n\nLet me conclude my speech, calling upon the President to empathize with the suffering masses and to adequately cushion the low-income families from the sudden increase in prices of essential foodstuffs."
