    "description": "Hansard of February 09, 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1710928762052246.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2024-02-09-2024-02-09-0219",
    "chunk_index": 219,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "6cf9e9ef45759aa33bdedde3ea7d81a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1640,
    "chunk_text": "357 358\n\n[ \u0dbb\u0dd4 [\u0db1\u0dca\u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dbd \u0dc1\u0dc1\u0dda\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca [\u0dc1\u0dad\u0da7]\n\n7]74 \u0dc1\u0db4\u0db3\u0dca\u0dc0\u0da7\u0dbb\u0dd2 ]9\n\nThe President\u2019s Address clearly demonstrated his leadership acumen and his dedication to steering our country towards development on the global stage.\n\nDuring this time, Sri Lanka found itself isolated and labelled as economically insolvent by international financial institutions. Inflation surged, triggering an economic downturn which pushed many poor families to the brink of despair. However, within a span of less than two years, the President managed to reverse that dire situation. Our once troubled economy is now on the path to recovery, with numerous pressing issues being addressed to provide relief to those affected by the crisis.\n\nSecuring a loan from the International Monetary Fund - IMF- stands as one of the significant accomplishments of the President.\n\nThe tourism sector which had collapsed entirely is now rebounding and is poised to become a vital source of foreign exchange for the country. Investors from India, other neighbouring countries and from Europe are showing interest in investing in Sri Lanka. The credit for fostering such a conducive environment undoubtedly belongs to our esteemed President. It is doubtful that anyone other than President Ranil Wickremesinghe could have achieved such a remarkable progress. At the time of our President assuming office, Sri Lanka possessed minimal foreign reserves. Today, we have boosted an ample reserve. Comparing the current situation with that of 2021 and 2022, it reveals a stark contrast; the bankrupt economy has transformed into a thriving one."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
