    "date_str": "2024-02-09",
    "description": "Hansard of February 09, 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1710928762052246.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2024-02-09-2024-02-09-0220",
    "chunk_index": 220,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "cff8f28974dcdbe72f82ae5429d60256",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1951,
    "chunk_text": "The tourism sector which had collapsed entirely is now rebounding and is poised to become a vital source of foreign exchange for the country. Investors from India, other neighbouring countries and from Europe are showing interest in investing in Sri Lanka. The credit for fostering such a conducive environment undoubtedly belongs to our esteemed President. It is doubtful that anyone other than President Ranil Wickremesinghe could have achieved such a remarkable progress. At the time of our President assuming office, Sri Lanka possessed minimal foreign reserves. Today, we have boosted an ample reserve. Comparing the current situation with that of 2021 and 2022, it reveals a stark contrast; the bankrupt economy has transformed into a thriving one.\n\nRepeated elections within a short timeframe are unsustainable for our country. The pre-election period disrupts governmental functions, leading to inefficiencies and waste of resources. Consolidating elections into a single parliamentary election as opposed to separate presidential and parliamentary contests would mitigate these challenges and reduce expenditure. The country cannot afford to have two elections within a period of six months. The moment the Presidential Election is called for, the Government machinery would not function properly, three months before and three months after the election. Then, the candidate who wins the Presidential\n\nElection would dissolve Parliament immediately because he would think his party could win the election and form a government. Again, when the Parliamentary Election is announced, the same thing is going to happen as was during the Presidential Election, which means three months before and three months after the election, the State machinery would not function properly. So, again, an invaluable period of six months is going to be wasted without being used for the betterment of the country. In this way, one whole year would go to waste."
  },
