    "chunk_size_bytes": 2285,
    "chunk_text": "Election would dissolve Parliament immediately because he would think his party could win the election and form a government. Again, when the Parliamentary Election is announced, the same thing is going to happen as was during the Presidential Election, which means three months before and three months after the election, the State machinery would not function properly. So, again, an invaluable period of six months is going to be wasted without being used for the betterment of the country. In this way, one whole year would go to waste.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dc5 \u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d94\u0db3\u0db8\u0dd2[\u0da7\u0da7 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dba\u0d9c\u0dad \u0da7\u0d9a\u0dbd \u0d85\u0dc0 \u0db1\u0dca, \u0dbb\u0dd4 [\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dd2[\u0db1\u0dd2. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d92.\u0d91\u0da0\u0dca.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0dc6\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dd2 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8f.\u0b8e\u0b9a\u0bcd.\u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bcc\u0bb8\u0bbf) (The Hon. A.H.M. Fowzie) Give me one more minute, Sir.\n\nThe President says that the year 2024 would be a promising year and that in 2025, the country would set a remarkable progress economically. How can we achieve this goal if investors are not coming to our country? Investors would not come because the political situation of the country is questionable; they would not take any risk by investing here. The economy would crash and would go back to the state it was in when the President took office two years before, where we had major shortages of fuel, food and other basic items.\n\nI strongly hold onto my position or stance that the existing presidential system must be abolished because Presidents, in the past, made arbitrary decisions without consulting Parliament or the Cabinet, which resulted in many tragedies that affected the country tremendously. After a President\u2019s retirement from office, the Government has to spend a huge amount of money for the maintenance of the luxury bungalow and the security given to him while paying him a monthly pension. Actually, with this system, nothing good is going to happen to the country\u2019s economy other than wasting State funds which could be made use of for the country\u2019s economic advancement."
  },
