    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab (\u0dab\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0db4 \u0d9a\u0dbb \u0db8\u0da2\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b9a\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0bb5\u0bc0\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0b9a\u0b95\u0bb0) (The Hon.(Dr.) Sarath Weerasekera) Hon. Presiding Member, before I speak on the subject under discussion, let me take this opportunity to give a very important message to this august Assembly. That is about an interesting and valuable article written by Mr. Dharshan Weerasekera, a Sri Lankan lawyer pursuing his LLM Degree at the University of Colombo, published in the prestigious Groningen Journal of International Law.\n\nDharshan\u2019s article is titled \u201cA UNHRC Resolution of Questionable Legality on Sri Lanka and its Importance as a Catalyst for Future UN Reform\u201d. In it, he proves that these Resolutions sponsored by the United States and its allies are not to foster peace and reconciliation in Sri\n\n669 670\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9c\u0dbd\u0dca \u0dad \u0dca\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0daf\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dca \u0db8\u0db1\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n]0]4 \u0dc1\u0db4\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dd2 ]1\n\nLanka, but innovative tactics to enable them to intervene in the internal affairs of weak nations by using the UNHRC as a conduit. Also, I must say that we see how even the present US Ambassador to Sri Lanka interferes in every domestic affair in our country, violating the Vienna Convention. In that state of affairs, I congratulate our President Ranil Wickremesinghe for keeping her in the proper place when she tried to find fault with the manner in which the \u201caragalaya\u201d was dispersed. Dharshan also proves that in pursuing these Resolutions, the UNHRC has violated the fundamental principles of the Charter of UN as well as UNHRC\u2019s founding documents. He says that it is in the interest of all persons who value the rule of law in international affairs that he brings out what exactly has happened so that they could advocate for the relevant reforms in order to prevent the United Nations from losing its credibility any further."
