    "md5": "7b6bad0c6bb81cf77729bbeb41224cac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1834,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, farmers in Sri Lanka face numerous challenges, including lack of access to credit, fluctuating market prices, inadequate infrastructure and difficulties in obtaining quality inputs such as seeds and fertilizers. Additionally, unpredictable weather patterns and natural disasters pose risks to crop yields and livelihoods. Fishermen also encounter various issues, such as competition from industrial fishing vessels, overfishing, declining fish stocks and environmental degradation. Also lack of proper equipment, safety measures and market access further hinder the fishing industry\u2019s sustainable development.\n\nSir, rebuilding and recovering from the conflict\u2019s impact in the Northern and the Eastern regions is still ongoing, necessitating reconciliation efforts, infrastructure development and economic revitalization for sustainable progress. To address those challenges, targeted poverty alleviation programmes, improved infrastructure, access to markets, job creation, education, healthcare and social services are crucial. Strengthening community-based initiatives and ensuring the participation of marginalized groups in development efforts are essential for promoting sustainable development and enhancing the well-being of the population in those regions.\n\nSir, corruption remains a prevalent issue in Sri Lanka with reports of corrupt practices in government institutions, public services, procurement processes and other sectors. Corruption undermines the rule of law, erodes public trust in the Government and distorts market mechanisms. It hinders economic growth by increasing the cost of doing business, deterring foreign investments\n\n749 750\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da9:\u0dbd \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dc1\u0d9c\u0ddc\u0db4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n]0]4 \u0dc1\u0db4\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0daf\u0dbb\u0dd2 ]1\n\nand fostering an environment of cronyism and rent-seeking behavior."
  },
